bas-c (1.1.0) testing; urgency=medium

  * Align packaging with zephyr/clib: LICENSE, AsciiDoc man pages, meson
    version/license metadata, debian source format/copyright, and multi-
    distro packaging stubs.
  * stackdump: honor STACKDUMP=highlight|raw|fast for crash-handler dump
    mode; quiet install banner.
  * Wire L1 gettext locales (es_MX, ar) and bas i18n init in unit-test
    mains.
  * Add GitHub Actions release-packages workflow: Debian/RHEL matrix via
    Docker, attach zips to the GitHub Release, optional s1 dput/rpm
    publish.
  * Fix packaging/rpm/bas-c.spec: RHEL BuildRequires and ship
    libraries/headers in %files.
  * meson: treat missing includes(1) as optional so clean Debian builds
    work.
  * CI: install peer Build-Depends from REPODEB_URL (repodeb_aptly);
    anonymous HTTP publish.
  * RPM %files: only ship doc/libbas-c (matches meson install_dir).
  * mingw: skip cleanly when cross glib-2.0 is unavailable.
  * RPM %files: include libbas-c.a and all locale *.mo (variant
    catalogs).

